<title>RUSSIA: Two Russian airforce generals killed in air crash.</title>
<headline>Two Russian airforce generals killed in air crash.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Russian airforce generals were among six people killed on Wednesday when an MI-8 military helicopter crashed north of the Siberian city of Chita.</p>
<p>An air force spokesman named the dead on Thursday as Lieutenant-General Dmitry Kutsekon, the commander of the 23rd Air Force, and his chief-of-staff, Major-General Boris Batura.</p>
<p>An inquiry into the incident is under way.</p>
